Z||000017||LZeitgeist||09-13-2001||06:41 PM||||Black88GT - <P>You forget that THEY DON'T THINK LIKE WE DO.<P>To them, dying for the love of their God and their country is a SURE, STRAIGHT IMMEDIATE TICKET TO HEAVEN.<P>Another thought that has been nagging me is that right now, it *appears* that the US thinks it's bin Laden. So, we take him out. Boom, he's gone. Then, Saddam speaks up, declares that it *wasn't* in fact bin Laden that did it, but HIM, and accuses us of killing an innocent man, and completely humiliating us in front of the entire globe. (Or reverse the two roles if you wish.)<P>All these years, these terrorists have wanted not necessarily to kill us, but to HUMILIATE us. To get us right in the middle of our "overblown" (to them, at least) pride. To prove to the world that we are not worthy of being considered a superpower.<P>Our continued mistake is that instead of thinking like they do, we base our decisions on what makes sense to OUR basis of logic - OUR basis of morality - OUR basis of 'fair play', and right and wrong. In order to BEAT them, we have to think LIKE them. There is no other way. <P>As I said in another post, THEY made their bed. It is now OUR CHOICE whether or not to force them to lie in it or not. Unless the US Government does something different this time than what they have historicallly done in similar situations, nothing will change. Whoever did this will live, and they will do it again the next time they get the chance.||||reg||1
Z||000018||Urchin||09-13-2001||06:55 PM||||It is also possible that they (Saddam, Bin Laden, or both) were not counting on any retalitory measures by the U.S.  Perhaps they figured that they would get away with it and viewing it as an act of terrorism and nothing more.  This may be an outlandish assumption, but as many have said...  why would any of these people intentionally wage war with the U.S.  This act was well planned and no one has claimed responsibilty.  You would think that if they intended on going to war with the U.S. that they would admit involvement with the events.  Does any of this make sense?  I think they intended on "pay back" and nothing more.  Perhaps there initial plan has blown up in there face.  Also consider that one of the planes was apparently intended to target the whitehouse.  This being the case, that brings up even more questions.  Maybe they figured if the president was taken out that they could take advantage of the U.S. in a vulnerable state.  Just some more thoughts...<P>A little more food for thought:  This is not the first time a claim on Bin Laden's life has been made by a president.  The same can be said for Saddam Huisane (sp?).  I suppose this situation is a little different than in the past, but it may take foot soldiers going in and tracking him down.<p>[This message has been edited by Urchin (edited 09-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000019||stsmithgt||09-13-2001||06:56 PM||||I suppose Butthead Laden and Saddamy Hinsane are both involve some way.  their plan is valid.  We blow them up, then we rebuild them to take advantage of their resources as if they will change after the punishment.  I say destroy one of the same targets they were after, their economy.  Flatten them and let them suffer in the terror inflicted from the country drowning in poverty and disease.  Our allies around them can scoop up the remains that are worth keeping as long as we get Bin Ladens bank roll that can more than cover our expenses$$$.(not the loss of life though)  <BR>I know this idea isn't too realistic, but it felt good to type it out. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firework.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>My work of art.(in progress.)    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/carpicsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
