Z||000026||sqoach||09-14-2001||01:59 AM||||LZ, I don't think we would be humiliated by eliminating bin Laden, then find out it wasn't him behind this. (though I think he has a huge part in it) We've been after him for years. There's been a $5 mil reward for his capture. He is a terrorist. Bush seeks to wipe out terrorism. Taking out bin Laden would be a good thing, not humiliating. This is just an opinion, so don't get mad.<P>Another opinion. I think if we should strike, it better be pretty damn soon. I think we have waited too long already. They have heard that we will retaliate, so that gives them time to get their sh!t together. I heard a reporter ask a colonel on CNN(?) what they plan to do. And he stated they will most likely bomb Afghanistan(sp?)! I think this was yesterday evening. Then the reporter goes on to say, "I'd hate to live in one of those countries right now." Or something to that effect. I mean, come on! You just told them what we're planning! Don't give them time to get ready!<BR>Anyway, that's just my thought.<P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif">         <BR>^^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^^<BR><LI><FONT SIZE="1">84 SE (FOR SALE)*sale pending*<BR><LI>85 Coupe (parts car)($50)*sale pending*<BR><LI>86 SC (FOR SALE)</FONT>||||reg||1
